At first glance, this test looks confusing but I think it is operating
as expected.  Lines 2 and 3 are concatenated into one logical line
by readline() itself, resulting in
Here is another @\, and then yet another ... @\.

m2 tries to parse everything between the @ signs as a function,
and dutifully reports (errors) that "\," (i.e., param[0] == "\,")
is not a defined function name.
